<title>UK: IBCA says rates Baden-Wurttemberg notes.</title>
<headline>IBCA says rates Baden-Wurttemberg notes.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>IBCA, the European credit rating agency, said on Tuesday it assigned a long-term rating of AAA to the Baden-Wurttemberg L-Finance NV 1.0 billion franc 4.125 percent/TEC10 -1.17 percent notes 2007 issue, guaranteed by Landeskreditbank Baden-Wurttemberg (L-Bank).</p>
<p>IBCA said in a statement it also assigned a long-term rating of AAA to the L-Bank 200 billion lire 7.3 percent notes 2006 issue under its five billion U.S. dollar EMTN programme.</p>
<p>&quot;The ratings are based on the implied federal German guarantee for the obligations of L-Bank,&quot; IBCA said.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 6176</p>
